<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leopoldine Diploma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1691">1691</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Diploma Leopoldinum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Leopoldine Diploma was the charter issued by Emperor Leopold I in 1691 that settled the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule after the Ottoman retreat. It confirmed the rights of the Transylvanian estates, the privileges of the three recognised nations and the four accepted religions, while placing the principality under a governor answerable to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>. It remained the basis of Transylvania's constitution until 1848.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leopoldine-diploma.jpg" alt="Leopoldine Diploma" width="320" height="366" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Leopold I, Holy Roman Emperor · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diploma_Leopoldinum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
